[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4978412546","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/121024#issuecomment-4978412546","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121024","id":4978412546,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABKLyMAg","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-15T08:20:40Z","updated_at":"2026-07-15T08:20:40Z","body":"Instead of allowing items to be placed on top of a sticky element during drag, I think it would also be acceptable to hide the sticky element while dragging.\n\nThe scroll container tree scrolls when you drag an object to the top or bottom edge. Currently, it does scroll when dragging an object above a sticky element, but the sticky element makes it difficult to see what is at the scroll destination. Especially with operations like a laptop trackpad, where you cannot scroll and drag simultaneously, the current situation causes a regression in usability when trying to properly place objects in areas hidden by a sticky element.","author